 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "A book for «آيات للسائلين» (after Yusuf's name; a gold burst could read as the stars of the dream). The plot (8-10) has no plate: no killing, well, child or caravan drawn. Their charge «إن أبانا لفي ضلال مبين» keeps As-Sa'di's «من غير موجب نراه» (their view, in their words). 9:10-14 shows As-Sa'di's «فقدموا العزم على التوبة قبل صدور الذنب منهم تسهيلا لفعله», so their «قوما صالحين» is not read as praise. STAGING v4: Both chapters in the desert by day (the family lived in the badiya, 12:100). c1 (7): Yusuf (blue drop labelled Yusuf) and his brothers, three faceless men in plain robes (people, not the dark robes of deniers: they repent later, 97-98; three is the series' sign for a group; they are never numbered), a book plate for signs for those who ask (7:6). c2 (8-10): the brothers alone, talking among themselves (both tafsirs: فيما بينهم): the same three men stand close together, drawn as two actors so that they can answer each other (8:2, 8:9, 9:1, 9:6); nobody else is on stage and nobody speaks to an empty side. 10: one of them speaks (10:2, both tafsirs: a speaker from among them) and shakes his head on do not kill (10:4); the well, Yusuf, any harm and the travellers are never drawn; a footsteps plate for the travellers who would pick him up (10:13). No close-up on any figure while Yusuf's name is recited (8:3, 9:2, 10:6): the camera is wide each time; it closes in on them only later in the verse (9:8, 10:12). Cover: the brothers conferring (title: the brothers' envy). For the human reviewer: 3 figures = a group, not their number (the brothers are never counted; review 12a M1)."
 },
